WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.386
Lockfiles help turn dependency resolution
into something the team can review.

2
00:00:06.466 --> 00:00:09.102
package.json often allows ranges,

3
00:00:09.182 --> 00:00:14.453
while package-lock.json records the tree
that npm actually selected.

4
00:00:14.533 --> 00:00:20.683
That resolved tree includes transitive
packages the team may never name directly.

5
00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:23.838
When a pull request changes the lockfile,

6
00:00:23.918 --> 00:00:27.256
reviewers can inspect which packages
moved,

7
00:00:27.336 --> 00:00:30.763
whether a major version appeared
indirectly,

8
00:00:30.843 --> 00:00:35.587
and whether the update matches the stated
reason for the change.

9
00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:41.992
npm install is convenient during
development because it can update the lockfile when

10
00:00:42.072 --> 00:00:43.741
dependencies change.

11
00:00:43.821 --> 00:00:47.775
npm ci is designed for clean, repeatable
automation.

12
00:00:47.855 --> 00:00:53.653
It removes the existing node_modules
directory, installs from the lockfile,

13
00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:58.741
and fails when package.json and
package-lock.json are out of sync.

14
00:00:58.821 --> 00:01:04.795
That makes npm ci a better default for
CI/CD because the build should prove what is

15
00:01:04.875 --> 00:01:10.146
already recorded, not silently resolve a
new tree during the pipeline.

16
00:01:10.226 --> 00:01:14.443
Reproducible installs are not the same as
safe installs.

17
00:01:14.523 --> 00:01:19.970
A lockfile can reproduce a vulnerable
dependency, an untrusted package,

18
00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:23.652
or an unsafe script just as reliably as a
good one.

19
00:01:23.732 --> 00:01:28.476
The security value comes from combining
lockfiles with review,

20
00:01:28.556 --> 00:01:34.794
audit triage, controlled updates, clean CI
environments, and release discipline.

21
00:01:34.874 --> 00:01:39.091
Think of the lockfile as evidence and
control over drift,

22
00:01:39.171 --> 00:01:43.300
not as a guarantee that every dependency
is acceptable.
